{{> judge-opening}}

JUDGMENT POINT: THE ARTICLE'S LANGUAGE (kogaki#1417): `language` in the input is the one language the article is written in, declared by the Audience file; write every proposition you compose in it, and keep in English only the keys and ids the record's shape fixes. compose ONE APEX for EACH connected component of the RelationalStructure in the input, `components` -- each one a higher-order relation connects and with two or more top-level relations, since a component no higher-order relation connects is not a Thesis candidate and a component with one top carries that top as its apex (kogaki#1773): each component lists its relations and higher-order relations with their `name` and their `holds` in Role names, its `top` -- the higher-order relations no other relates, or its relations where it has none -- and the claims it is read from, `claims`. The apex is the Thesis an article built on that component alone argues: one sentence, in the claims' own words and naming the claims' objects -- never over Role ids, so it carries no `{<id>}` -- stating the connection the component's top-level relations together make, which no single claim states. `component` names the component's id, `name` is one short snake_case word that no Role, relation or higher-order relation of the components carries, `relates` names exactly the component's `top` ids, and the apex carries no `id`, which is minted when it is adopted, and no `from`: the apex is the one connection no claim states (kogaki#1772). Answer the apex record and nothing else.
REQUIRED RECORD SHAPE: ONE record AT THE RECORD'S OWN ROOT carrying exactly `apexes` -- a list of `{ "component": <a component id of the input>, "name": <one short snake_case word, no name of the structure>, "relates": [<the component's `top` ids>], "holds": <one sentence, the Thesis> }`, one per component of the input.
WHAT IS REFUSED: a key the record or an apex does not declare, or a declared key missing; an apex naming a component the input does not carry, or two apexes naming one; an apex carrying `id` or `from`; a `name` that is not one snake_case word or is already a name of the structure; `relates` other than exactly the component's `top`, refused naming the component; a `holds` that is empty or carries `{<id>}`; and a component carrying no apex. The refusal is put back into your next round verbatim with your answer.

